  "details": "The button is most often used to change avatar. As such, the old \"Change into avatar[s]\" text on it was perfect.\nWhile it's true that the button currently does also change fallback (if it was modified), wording the button specifically for that rather rare case feels like a very odd choice to me, especially with the current, very-final-and-no-going-back wording of \"confirm this choice\" that mentions neither avatars nor change.",
